I've read conflicting info about this issue. Some people say: get MR,
stand on ^poly, whistle, and displace a pet into it... and repeat often
until you've got (a) good pet(s). Others say (and the 3.3.1 praying
spoiler appendix has this): Displacing a pet onto a trap gives you a -3
alignment penalty... so don't do it often, and be careful praying
afterward.

After perusing the 3.4.3 code backward from "adjalign(-3);" (though I'm
not very familiar with nethack's code yet) it appears to me that the only
time you get a -3 alignment penalty is if you displace your pet into a
trap in which they *become trapped* (bear trap, pit, etc.) -- thus ^poly
would not. Wizmode testing seems to bear this out. Is this right?

